WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:07.350
There’s no business like show business—but in Los Angeles, it feels like there’s no business at all.
没有哪一行比得上演艺业，可在洛杉矶，感觉根本就没有生意可做。

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:24.880
If that sounds melodramatic, consider this: The Art Directors Guild, a labor union representing about 3,000 film workers, has suspended a training program and issued a statement explaining that “we cannot in good conscience encourage you to pursue our profession.”
如果这听起来有些夸张，那不妨看看这件事：代表约3000名电影从业者的美术指导工会已经暂停了一项培训计划，并发表声明解释说：“凭良心讲，我们无法鼓励你们从事我们这一行。”

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:32.330
This is a reaction to Hollywood’s decline, which is reaching a critical point for the industry and Southern California.
这是对好莱坞衰落作出的反应，而对这个行业和南加州来说，这种衰落正走到一个临界点。

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:40.180
Production has been slipping away from Hollywood since the 1950s, but the effects have never been more apparent than at present.
自20世纪50年代以来，影视制作就一直在从好莱坞流失，但其影响从未像现在这样明显。

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:50.330
Other regions in the United States, Canada and Europe have steadily increased incentives to attract TV shows and movies, leaving California in the dust.
美国、加拿大和欧洲的其他地区一直在稳步加大激励力度，以吸引电视节目和电影，把加州远远甩在了后面。

00:00:51.130 --> 00:01:04.540
Georgia offers up to 30% in transferable tax credits on film and TV production costs, including an additional 10% increase on the base tax credit if the project includes a Georgia promotional logo.
佐治亚州为影视制作成本提供最高达30%的可转让税收抵免，其中，如果项目带有佐治亚州的宣传标识，还可在基础税收抵免之上额外提高10%。

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:14.930
Even as California lost a huge volume of production to other locations, there was still plenty of film production taking place in Los Angeles before this year.
即便加州有大量影视制作流失到了其他地方，今年之前，洛杉矶仍有很多电影在拍摄。

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:22.350
We were kept afloat by “peak TV”—the glut of content that was required by the explosion of streaming services.
让我们撑下来的是“巅峰电视”，即流媒体服务爆炸式增长所需要的过量内容。

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:25.880
But 2022 was the peak of peak TV.
但2022年是“巅峰电视”的顶峰。

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:40.240
Back then platforms such as Netflix, Amazon and Apple TV hemorrhaged billions of dollars to generate content to attract new subscribers, resulting in 633 scripted series being released that year.
当时，Netflix、亚马逊和Apple TV等平台为了产出内容以吸引新订户，烧掉了数十亿美元，结果那一年推出了633部剧本类剧集。

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:56.780
As the streamers’ emphasis changed from subscriber growth to profitability, prices for the services went up and the number of new shows went down to 481 released in 2023, with the number expected to dip into the 300s within a few years.
随着流媒体平台的重心从订户增长转向盈利，这些服务的价格上涨了，新剧集的数量则下降到2023年推出的481部，预计几年之内还会降到300多部。

00:01:57.580 --> 00:02:07.470
If productions in Southern California dip below a critical level for too long, the industry’s essential talent will drift away along with enormous sums of revenue.
如果南加州的影视制作量跌到临界水平以下的时间过长，这个行业不可或缺的人才就会逐渐流失，巨额收入也会随之流走。

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:19.710
Persuading studios to film here would become much more challenging if we couldn’t offer a deep bench of local film workers, on-screen talent and local businesses that support the entertainment industry.
如果我们拿不出一大批本地电影从业者、幕前人才和支持娱乐产业的本地企业，要说服制片公司来这里拍摄就会困难得多。

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:27.960
That’s why the California Film Commission and its Los Angeles counterpart, FilmLA, now should act, before it’s too late.
正因如此，加州电影委员会及其在洛杉矶的对应机构FilmLA现在就应该采取行动，以免为时已晚。

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:37.490
These agencies and other government bodies should dramatically improve incentives to keep our current shows and attract new productions to Los Angeles.
这些机构和其他政府部门应当大幅改善激励措施，以留住我们现有的剧集，并把新的影视项目吸引到洛杉矶来。

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:41.980
Let’s go on with the show…and make sure the show doesn’t go on without us.
让演出继续下去吧……同时要确保，这场演出不会撇下我们继续上演。
